#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186322782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc92887d-99d9-555e-b40c-0f2a8cfe6088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{5x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322784} {:answer/id #uuid "1c854187-c69d-511b-bf1d-22b1420dffb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{5x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322785} {:answer/id #uuid "3b1e5dec-e6c4-5bb1-bf0b-abdcefca5d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{5x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322786} {:answer/id #uuid "b03d6d44-84f1-5dba-9479-2420747d3099" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{5x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322787} {:answer/id #uuid "cffb20fa-7eba-5d2b-b681-2ebb1ded0c5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{5x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b1e5dec-e6c4-5bb1-bf0b-abdcefca5d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{5x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322786} :answer-field/id #uuid "90c95b81-784e-545f-b0aa-64791a51987d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "06c70e02-23ad-5443-a5fb-c80cbe357a8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-10457" :question/problem "$\\int (5{cos}^{2}⁡2x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =2x$, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡2x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5{cos}^{2}⁡2x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int [5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{5}{2}x-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{5x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
